1
00:00:05,250 --> 00:02:05,250
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:09,383 --> 00:02:12,845
Episode 91

3
00:02:27,085 --> 00:02:28,635
Alaaddin.

4
00:02:33,655 --> 00:02:35,715
Wake up, brother.

5
00:02:45,525 --> 00:02:46,835
Alaaddin!

6
00:02:50,975 --> 00:02:52,485
Come on, Alaaddin!

7
00:02:52,605 --> 00:02:54,005
Wake up!

8
00:03:01,995 --> 00:03:04,515
We need to get out of here.

9
00:03:12,415 --> 00:03:14,535
This is so bad, brother.

10
00:03:14,915 --> 00:03:17,155
We are a trump card in the hands of
the infidel.

11
00:03:17,395 --> 00:03:19,035
We won't be for too long.

12
00:03:19,795 --> 00:03:21,395
We will escape, brother.

13
00:03:21,875 --> 00:03:23,125
Come on!

14
00:03:30,805 --> 00:03:33,135
No soldiers are around.

15
00:03:35,395 --> 00:03:37,255
My Allah, give me strength.

16
00:03:52,615 --> 00:03:55,235
What is this?
Are you trying to escape?

17
00:03:56,825 --> 00:03:59,375
Look, some fun for us.

18
00:04:04,615 --> 00:04:07,615
The man who could bend this iron
would not have been captured.

19
00:04:08,475 --> 00:04:09,855
Don't cause trouble, kid!

20
00:04:10,055 --> 00:04:14,115
Neither iron nor walls can hold the Turk,
you infidel!

21
00:04:14,555 --> 00:04:17,024
Open this lock so that I can show you.

22
00:04:21,605 --> 00:04:25,525
Does a dog ever enter a wolf's den,
brother?

23
00:04:27,895 --> 00:04:30,275
If it is to die, it does, brother.

24
00:04:33,485 --> 00:04:35,605
You will see now!

25
00:04:44,935 --> 00:04:47,055
I know what to do with you!

26
00:04:48,535 --> 00:04:51,885
After Osman is killed, it will be your
turn anyway.

27
00:04:57,955 --> 00:04:59,835
Allah!

28
00:04:59,875 --> 00:05:01,315
Allah!

29
00:05:04,545 --> 00:05:06,435
Did you see my power now?

30
00:05:12,275 --> 00:05:13,675
You dogs!

31
00:05:13,815 --> 00:05:15,015
Let us go!

32
00:05:15,135 --> 00:05:16,885
Let us go!

33
00:05:25,805 --> 00:05:27,335
You dogs!

34
00:06:11,025 --> 00:06:13,165
My Osman Bey won't let you get away
with this!

35
00:06:13,185 --> 00:06:15,805
He will destroy your castle upon you when
he hears this!

36
00:06:15,805 --> 00:06:17,905
Osman will die too! There is no hope
for you!

37
00:06:17,905 --> 00:06:19,995
Shut up and at least don't die tired!

38
00:06:35,285 --> 00:06:37,835
Come on! Enough resting!

39
00:06:38,195 --> 00:06:39,995
We have to set off!

40
00:06:40,055 --> 00:06:41,835
Our duty is hard!

41
00:06:41,975 --> 00:06:43,105
Alps!

42
00:06:43,395 --> 00:06:45,845
Keep your eyes open and be careful!

43
00:06:46,205 --> 00:06:50,615
We are going to a wedding but our swords
will be sharp.

44
00:06:50,935 --> 00:06:52,805
We are going to conquer!
Come on!

45
00:06:54,535 --> 00:06:57,685
Come on, sisters! Come on!

46
00:06:58,525 --> 00:07:00,105
People are coming!

47
00:07:00,295 --> 00:07:02,415
People are coming!

48
00:07:03,395 --> 00:07:05,415
I hope this ends up well.

49
00:07:11,765 --> 00:07:13,055
Bala!

50
00:07:19,945 --> 00:07:21,405
-Malhun!
-Bala!

51
00:07:21,705 --> 00:07:23,115
They kidnapped the children!

52
00:07:23,365 --> 00:07:25,045
What? Who? When?

53
00:07:25,285 --> 00:07:28,205
There is no time. They took the kids
to Bilecik!

54
00:07:28,355 --> 00:07:30,475
-Let's go to Bilecik then. Come on!
-Come on!

55
00:07:31,175 --> 00:07:33,415
Osman Bey is coming!

56
00:07:49,735 --> 00:07:51,125
Osman!

57
00:07:51,215 --> 00:07:52,745
They kidnapped the children!

58
00:07:52,805 --> 00:07:55,395
I know, Malhun.
I know.

59
00:07:56,015 --> 00:07:58,315
What if something happens to our children,
Osman?

60
00:07:58,415 --> 00:07:59,995
It won't.

61
00:08:00,065 --> 00:08:01,945
They attacked Kosses as well.

62
00:08:01,955 --> 00:08:03,995
But he went to the tribe now.

63
00:08:05,415 --> 00:08:08,415
If they had wanted to try to kill our
children...

64
00:08:08,665 --> 00:08:11,225
...they wouldn't take them to Bilecik.

65
00:08:11,635 --> 00:08:13,185
What is their intention?

66
00:08:13,255 --> 00:08:15,335
To use them against us?

67
00:08:15,525 --> 00:08:17,475
They were going to kill us at the Castle.

68
00:08:17,625 --> 00:08:20,755
They are doing this so that our children
don't seek revenge.

69
00:08:21,075 --> 00:08:23,625
They have known us for so long.

70
00:08:23,865 --> 00:08:26,425
Of course, they know we won't go
there unprepared.

71
00:08:26,485 --> 00:08:30,525
That's why they want to hit us at
our weak spot.

72
00:08:32,683 --> 00:08:36,794
But I will neither leave my children to
them...

73
00:08:37,095 --> 00:08:39,615
...nor let them live!

74
00:08:39,875 --> 00:08:42,945
All right, then! Let's destroy Bilecik
upon them!

75
00:08:43,015 --> 00:08:44,825
No.

76
00:08:46,015 --> 00:08:47,545
Malhun...

77
00:08:47,565 --> 00:08:49,395
...we won't act out of pain.

78
00:08:51,635 --> 00:08:53,765
We will act by our minds.

79
00:09:24,325 --> 00:09:27,015
Osman is dead.

80
00:09:35,105 --> 00:09:38,435
Osman will sit right here.

81
00:09:39,335 --> 00:09:42,765
And the assassins will be here.

82
00:09:42,845 --> 00:09:46,505
There will be also Justinyanus' soldiers
besides yours.

83
00:09:46,725 --> 00:09:49,785
What difference does it make where
Osman sits?

84
00:09:51,345 --> 00:09:53,955
I like a precaution.

85
00:09:54,875 --> 00:09:59,235
You taught me not to belittle anyone
in war, Master.

86
00:10:00,965 --> 00:10:03,235
I won't leave an open door.

87
00:10:03,435 --> 00:10:06,885
You say the most right words, Nikola.

88
00:10:08,135 --> 00:10:11,155
Aya Nikola, Master Arius...

89
00:10:11,375 --> 00:10:12,965
...this is the Bilecik Castle.

90
00:10:13,085 --> 00:10:16,755
But the history will remember this castle
as the graves of Turk beys.

91
00:10:16,885 --> 00:10:18,695
I have no doubt.

92
00:10:19,675 --> 00:10:22,475
Jugglers outside, actors, musicians...

93
00:10:22,745 --> 00:10:25,835
...they all have a dagger on their belts.

94
00:10:25,925 --> 00:10:27,815
They are thirsty for Turkish blood.

95
00:10:28,005 --> 00:10:31,525
Did you tell them about their actual goal?

96
00:10:33,295 --> 00:10:34,755
Of course, I didn't.

97
00:10:35,635 --> 00:10:38,245
I didn't say so that the information
wouldn't leak.

98
00:10:38,845 --> 00:10:41,965
They think is it only for precaution.

99
00:10:43,045 --> 00:10:47,095
When the war gets closer, they will find
out Bilecik will be covered in blood.

100
00:10:47,235 --> 00:10:49,505
But the Turks won't be full.

101
00:10:50,255 --> 00:10:51,805
They are fasting.

102
00:10:51,915 --> 00:10:55,015
Their sacred iftar will be their last
meal.

103
00:10:55,135 --> 00:10:58,195
Congratulations, Justinyanus!

104
00:10:58,355 --> 00:11:01,795
You are not a coward like your uncle
Rogatus.

105
00:11:02,115 --> 00:11:05,645
The peace that has ruled this land for
years with the order of Emperor...

106
00:11:05,855 --> 00:11:09,875
...ends tonight.

107
00:11:12,495 --> 00:11:14,195
What about Osman's children?

108
00:11:14,475 --> 00:11:15,765
What will happen to them?

109
00:11:15,975 --> 00:11:17,935
No one will touch them.

110
00:11:18,065 --> 00:11:19,745
They will wait for me.

111
00:11:20,255 --> 00:11:25,895
You can kill the alps, the women and even
Osman with pleasure.

112
00:11:30,215 --> 00:11:33,725
First, we will find out where our children
are.

113
00:11:34,645 --> 00:11:40,435
We won't fall into those dogs' traps who
want to kill us.

114
00:11:46,615 --> 00:11:48,655
Clearly, this is their move.

115
00:11:49,215 --> 00:11:51,305
You are right, Osman Bey.

116
00:11:51,395 --> 00:11:53,415
If we take precautions for the wedding...

117
00:11:53,425 --> 00:11:55,955
...they will want us to attack out of
anger.

118
00:11:56,015 --> 00:11:58,025
We will be cautious.

119
00:11:59,445 --> 00:12:01,055
What is your order, my Bey?

120
00:12:01,645 --> 00:12:04,655
We set off to take the Bilecik Castle.

121
00:12:06,165 --> 00:12:08,415
They abducted our children.

122
00:12:09,215 --> 00:12:11,155
They attacked Kosses.

123
00:12:14,195 --> 00:12:18,485
They want to secure their work.

124
00:12:19,845 --> 00:12:22,185
So will we!

125
00:12:23,985 --> 00:12:26,135
But we don't have anything to threaten
them.

126
00:12:26,475 --> 00:12:28,755
We are walking towards an ambush,
Osman Bey.

127
00:12:29,245 --> 00:12:30,995
How will we manage?

128
00:12:31,365 --> 00:12:33,525
You will see, Turgut Bey.

129
00:12:34,505 --> 00:12:38,565
My children will be with me before the sun
goes down.

130
00:12:40,835 --> 00:12:45,815
And Bilecik Castle will be our property.

131
00:12:47,365 --> 00:12:48,935
I hope so.

132
00:12:49,025 --> 00:12:50,215
I hope so, my Bey.

133
00:12:50,215 --> 00:12:51,915
I hope so.

134
00:12:59,685 --> 00:13:04,705
Justinyanus surprised us by telling us
what will happen in this hall...

135
00:13:05,005 --> 00:13:06,735
...Master Arius.

136
00:13:06,825 --> 00:13:09,795
Would you like to tell us what will happen
outside?

137
00:13:10,450 --> 00:13:12,630
When there will be a massacre in
the Castle...

138
00:13:12,685 --> 00:13:18,435
...when Osman's lineage ends Söğüt and
the tribe will be without a leader.

139
00:13:19,375 --> 00:13:21,915
-And Barkın--
-How?

140
00:13:23,075 --> 00:13:25,155
Isn't Barkın going to die?

141
00:13:26,755 --> 00:13:28,765
Justinyanus...

142
00:13:29,955 --> 00:13:34,095
...true loyalty is what everyone does not
know.

143
00:13:35,215 --> 00:13:37,405
Barkın has been loyal to me for years.

144
00:13:37,655 --> 00:13:39,405
Just like you have been.

145
00:13:41,035 --> 00:13:44,205
But Kosses is not like that, is he?

146
00:13:44,235 --> 00:13:46,055
Kosses is dead.

147
00:13:46,155 --> 00:13:47,545
Done.

148
00:13:50,005 --> 00:13:54,225
You, Justinyanus, will kill Osman and
the others.

149
00:13:54,735 --> 00:13:56,915
Barkım will take Söğüt.

150
00:13:57,435 --> 00:13:59,785
Söğüt got very wealthy.

151
00:14:01,365 --> 00:14:03,805
Osman got very wealthy.

152
00:14:04,925 --> 00:14:07,715
You will get your share as well.
Don't worry.

153
00:14:07,875 --> 00:14:12,025
And I will take my mines.

154
00:14:13,485 --> 00:14:16,825
What about you, Master Arius?
What will you do?

155
00:14:18,165 --> 00:14:23,865
I'll destroy his catapults before I turn
his skull into a slurry.

156
00:14:24,235 --> 00:14:26,305
I will destroy their weapons.

157
00:14:26,665 --> 00:14:29,625
Osman is making preparations for a
conquest.

158
00:14:30,155 --> 00:14:32,945
I will ruin his dream.

159
00:14:34,475 --> 00:14:38,725
Someone will take over the sanjaks
that the Turks consider sacred.

160
00:14:39,015 --> 00:14:40,745
Don't forget, Justinyanus.

161
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:43,615
You can't stop the Turks by killing them.

162
00:14:44,015 --> 00:14:50,155
You must put a man who will serve
you at their head.

163
00:14:51,575 --> 00:14:53,685
That man is Barkın.

164
00:14:56,235 --> 00:14:58,305
The war has begun.

165
00:14:59,375 --> 00:15:01,725
Only Osman doesn't know it.

166
00:15:02,835 --> 00:15:04,205
Come on.

167
00:15:14,485 --> 00:15:18,791
They set the trap in the Castle but
continue to attack on the road.

168
00:15:21,085 --> 00:15:23,625
Who else is on the road?

169
00:15:23,665 --> 00:15:25,425
The wedding convoy, my Bey.

170
00:15:26,085 --> 00:15:27,425
Right.

171
00:15:28,065 --> 00:15:30,385
Since they took our children as trumps...

172
00:15:31,905 --> 00:15:35,205
...we won't go there empty-handed.

173
00:15:39,540 --> 00:15:43,420
We will take Yarhisar Lord's daughter,
Holofira.

174
00:15:44,420 --> 00:15:46,260
We will raid the wedding convoy.

175
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,360
Well.

176
00:15:50,620 --> 00:15:52,500
Bala, Malhun...

177
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:57,860
...you will come to the castle with me
acting like you don't know about children.

178
00:15:59,980 --> 00:16:03,720
If you consider this appropriate then I
will hold my anger back...

179
00:16:04,060 --> 00:16:06,620
...and do as you order, Osman Bey.

180
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:10,920
We will wait for your sign.

181
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:12,320
Thank you.

182
00:16:12,660 --> 00:16:14,020
Thank you.

183
00:16:14,820 --> 00:16:16,400
Turgut Bey...

184
00:16:16,740 --> 00:16:19,300
...you will make the raid with alps.

185
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:21,960
Send Holofira to the tribe.

186
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:26,500
You will come to the Bilecik Castle with
her stepfather Basilius.

187
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:30,300
We can't enter the castle any other way.

188
00:16:30,380 --> 00:16:32,160
We will manage.

189
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:33,800
But the children...

190
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:36,560
...how will we save the children?

191
00:16:37,780 --> 00:16:40,500
There is someone who can find them and
inform us.

192
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:44,620
Who is it, my Bey.

193
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:49,620
My nephew, Aktemur.

194
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:15,060
Walk freely in your castle for now.

195
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:19,250
You won't even be able to take a step
when it becomes the Turks' property.

196
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:44,000
Holofira.

197
00:17:46,060 --> 00:17:48,340
I've raised you for these days.

198
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:51,860
You are left to me by your mother.

199
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:55,120
I married her for power.

200
00:17:57,620 --> 00:17:59,640
Even though you are not my daughter...

201
00:18:00,660 --> 00:18:02,240
...I accepted you.

202
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:09,200
You will do the same.

203
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:14,480
We only act for the sake of the sacred
Rome.

204
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:21,260
This marriage...

205
00:18:22,360 --> 00:18:24,860
...will make us even stronger.

206
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:28,440
I don't want to be strong.
I want to be happy.

207
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:26,540
Lord Basileus!

208
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:30,100
Get out of your hole!

209
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:10,940
What does this mean, Turgut Bey?

210
00:20:11,520 --> 00:20:15,040
After all these years of peace?

211
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:20,100
We will accompany you to Bilecik.

212
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:23,860
Let's see if the dagger against our throat
belongs to you.

213
00:20:25,460 --> 00:20:26,980
Damn it!

214
00:20:29,380 --> 00:20:30,960
Soldiers!

215
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:33,060
Alps!

216
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:47,300
You have nowhere to run, Lord!

217
00:20:51,100 --> 00:20:53,600
Your head seems to be heavy for your body,
Lord!

218
00:20:55,020 --> 00:20:56,900
Don't worry...

219
00:20:57,280 --> 00:20:59,560
...we will relieve you of that burden.

220
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:02,360
Attack!

221
00:21:28,110 --> 00:21:31,490
Be careful, Cerkutay!

222
00:21:34,980 --> 00:21:38,520
We have not fought side by side for a
long time and that's what you say?

223
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:40,340
Did you miss it?

224
00:21:43,080 --> 00:21:45,080
I missed the fight but...

225
00:21:45,440 --> 00:21:49,260
...I didn't miss your talking while
fighting, Cerkutay!

226
00:21:57,500 --> 00:22:01,620
Fine, then I will shut up and let my
swords talk!

227
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:07,700
Good for you!

228
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:37,080
Konuralp! The Lord is running away!

229
00:23:38,900 --> 00:23:40,700
Come on, little girl.

230
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:44,580
Come on.

231
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:55,640
Don't worry, we won't hurt you.

232
00:24:07,060 --> 00:24:09,060
Are you all like this?

233
00:24:10,740 --> 00:24:12,940
You are like my Mari.

234
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:16,600
It was unclear what she would do as well.

235
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:18,720
Alps!

236
00:24:19,940 --> 00:24:21,480
Boran!

237
00:24:24,300 --> 00:24:25,880
Protect the girl.

238
00:24:26,780 --> 00:24:28,820
I will take your father and return.

239
00:24:29,460 --> 00:24:32,700
Don't worry. Our brothers would never
hurt you.

240
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:37,980
I say I will accompany you.

241
00:25:38,060 --> 00:25:40,620
You are still trying to escape, Basilius.

242
00:25:50,780 --> 00:25:53,360
Will you stop us alone?

243
00:25:54,480 --> 00:25:56,300
You say so?

244
00:26:00,060 --> 00:26:01,880
Who said he was alone?

245
00:26:10,960 --> 00:26:12,680
Turgut Bey...

246
00:26:12,700 --> 00:26:14,700
...you will pay for this.

247
00:26:15,160 --> 00:26:17,660
We don't answer to snakes.

248
00:26:18,940 --> 00:26:21,080
We only ask!

249
00:26:21,940 --> 00:26:23,440
Attack!

250
00:26:43,980 --> 00:26:47,660
You've ruined all these years of peace!

251
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:52,140
You liar!

252
00:26:58,040 --> 00:27:01,720
You pretend to be innocent by standing
in front of me and saying peace!

253
00:27:02,440 --> 00:27:06,160
Say it, the wedding we planned was
supposed to be your funeral!

254
00:27:06,380 --> 00:27:07,700
Say it!

255
00:27:11,700 --> 00:27:14,100
I know how to make you tell the truth!

256
00:27:15,760 --> 00:27:17,880
In front of your daughter!

257
00:27:18,620 --> 00:27:20,000
Come on!

258
00:27:29,280 --> 00:27:30,660
Girl...

259
00:27:31,260 --> 00:27:33,040
...why are you crying?

260
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:37,180
We didn't kidnap you.

261
00:27:37,580 --> 00:27:39,080
We saved you.

262
00:27:40,540 --> 00:27:42,120
Don't be afraid.

263
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:44,120
Wipe your tears.

264
00:27:46,320 --> 00:27:49,320
The man who is your stepdad is
using you for his own purposes.

265
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:55,000
You are a stunning, brave girl.

266
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:15,520
Father!

267
00:28:18,360 --> 00:28:19,660
Tell her.

268
00:28:24,500 --> 00:28:25,800
Tell her!

269
00:28:32,820 --> 00:28:34,840
When I gave Holofira...

270
00:28:35,420 --> 00:28:38,540
...the Lord would make me a partner
in his trade.

271
00:28:40,960 --> 00:28:45,020
He also gave a lot of property from
his castle.

272
00:28:51,220 --> 00:28:52,740
Also...

273
00:28:53,580 --> 00:28:57,820
...it was a great move to kill you!

274
00:29:04,980 --> 00:29:07,500
This is your stepfather's true face.

275
00:29:11,180 --> 00:29:14,800
I'm no different than the animals
you raise for your benefit!

276
00:29:15,640 --> 00:29:19,180
The Turks you call our enemies treat me
better than you!

277
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:22,120
I hate you!

278
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:28,080
Aygül Hatun, you take Holofira to
the tribe.

279
00:29:28,320 --> 00:29:30,480
Then inform her aunt at once.

280
00:29:32,480 --> 00:29:34,040
Cerkutay...

281
00:29:34,140 --> 00:29:36,240
...you catch up with Osman Bey.

282
00:29:36,240 --> 00:29:37,740
Inform him about what happened.

283
00:29:37,820 --> 00:29:39,380
Come on, brother.

284
00:29:45,120 --> 00:29:46,880
This, Basileus is...

285
00:29:47,740 --> 00:29:49,560
...coming to the wedding with us!

286
00:29:51,540 --> 00:29:54,040
You are invited as well, you dog!

287
00:29:54,300 --> 00:29:55,840
You too!

288
00:30:18,740 --> 00:30:21,300
So you get the iron from here, Osman.

289
00:30:24,300 --> 00:30:26,800
Let's see where you forge all this iron.

290
00:30:27,840 --> 00:30:29,420
Did you load them all?

291
00:30:29,460 --> 00:30:31,020
Nothing is left!

292
00:30:31,020 --> 00:30:32,300
Good.

293
00:30:32,360 --> 00:30:33,900
Be very careful.

294
00:30:34,440 --> 00:30:35,800
Come on.

295
00:30:43,290 --> 00:30:47,040
We will be the breath of death on
their necks! Come on!

296
00:31:15,340 --> 00:31:17,040
My Bey, the mission is completed.

297
00:31:17,040 --> 00:31:18,560
We have the Lord.

298
00:31:18,610 --> 00:31:22,190
His daughter Holofira is going to
the tribe with alps, my Bey.

299
00:31:24,440 --> 00:31:28,660
Then let's go to our future estate!

300
00:31:29,540 --> 00:31:30,610
Come on!

301
00:31:47,780 --> 00:31:48,840
Bilecik Castle

302
00:31:48,840 --> 00:31:50,360
My soldiers!

303
00:31:51,650 --> 00:31:55,020
Many enemies have stood at the gates
of Rome to this day.

304
00:31:55,600 --> 00:32:00,470
Arabs, Mongols, and thousands of
barbarians.

305
00:32:02,350 --> 00:32:05,020
But they were never this close.

306
00:32:05,520 --> 00:32:07,470
We are the fire!

307
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:09,700
Whoever approaches us will perish!

308
00:32:12,260 --> 00:32:15,110
We bid farewell to the Turks permanently
tonight.

309
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:18,970
We have Osman's sons.

310
00:32:19,470 --> 00:32:21,700
He is coming to the wedding as well.

311
00:32:22,770 --> 00:32:25,050
We will hit them on the iftar table.

312
00:32:25,870 --> 00:32:29,720
We won't separate women, children or
old people.

313
00:32:31,420 --> 00:32:34,720
Everyone in the courtyard and the castle
will die!

314
00:32:39,450 --> 00:32:41,520
Who wants to shed Turkish blood?

315
00:32:41,520 --> 00:32:46,600
We do! We do! We do! We do!

316
00:32:46,850 --> 00:32:47,970
Death to the Turks!

317
00:32:48,020 --> 00:32:49,570
Death to the Turks!

318
00:32:49,570 --> 00:32:52,300
-For Great Caesar!
-For Great Caesar!

319
00:32:52,300 --> 00:32:58,920
-For Great Rome!
-For Great Rome!

320
00:33:03,500 --> 00:33:07,200
Sir, Osman and his people are coming.

321
00:33:11,750 --> 00:33:13,620
My friend Osman Bey.

322
00:33:13,770 --> 00:33:15,620
Let's welcome him.

323
00:33:27,785 --> 00:33:30,035
Tell me, Selcen Hatun...

324
00:33:30,035 --> 00:33:32,035
...who kidnapped my Shahzadas?

325
00:33:34,535 --> 00:33:37,585
Baysungur Alp said their faces were
covered, my Sheik.

326
00:33:37,735 --> 00:33:40,485
They look like those vile people
we knew years ago.

327
00:33:48,085 --> 00:33:49,855
I hope this is good.

328
00:33:49,855 --> 00:33:50,885
Bismillah.

329
00:33:50,885 --> 00:33:51,905
Mother.

330
00:33:51,905 --> 00:33:54,405
In the name of Allah!

331
00:33:57,155 --> 00:33:58,985
Get out!

332
00:34:00,435 --> 00:34:02,285
Open the way!

333
00:34:08,784 --> 00:34:11,554
Selcen Mother, Osman Bey sent him.

334
00:34:12,455 --> 00:34:15,005
Kosses is heavily wounded.
We must help.

335
00:34:17,554 --> 00:34:20,054
To the healing tent, Valiants! Come on!

336
00:34:20,105 --> 00:34:22,635
Come on!

337
00:34:22,635 --> 00:34:24,635
You, come here!

338
00:34:25,605 --> 00:34:29,155
Could my Osman find my grandchildren?

339
00:34:29,255 --> 00:34:31,755
He will soon, mother.

340
00:34:31,804 --> 00:34:33,534
Who did this?

341
00:34:33,534 --> 00:34:36,534
Orhan and Alaaddin's kidnapper was
the Lord of Yarhisar.

342
00:34:38,135 --> 00:34:40,235
The one who wounded Kosses is
his commander.

343
00:34:46,235 --> 00:34:47,804
My children!

344
00:34:49,735 --> 00:34:53,455
May my Allah protect our Shahzadas
from the cruelty of the enemy.

345
00:34:54,605 --> 00:34:55,955
Amen.

346
00:34:59,035 --> 00:35:01,105
-Hatuns.
-My Sheik.

347
00:35:01,105 --> 00:35:03,105
I will check on Kosses.

348
00:35:03,105 --> 00:35:07,605
You keep praying for our Shahzadas and
Kosses.

349
00:35:08,255 --> 00:35:10,255
Of course, my Sheik.

350
00:35:11,705 --> 00:35:13,085
Come on.

351
00:35:15,455 --> 00:35:17,485
Come on, mother. Let's go.

352
00:35:19,435 --> 00:35:22,485
My Allah, may you protect my children.

353
00:35:43,255 --> 00:35:45,335
How is he, Kumral Abdal?

354
00:35:46,055 --> 00:35:48,135
This is a terrible wound, my Sheik.

355
00:35:49,855 --> 00:35:52,205
But there is always hope.

356
00:36:00,805 --> 00:36:03,385
In the name of Allah!

357
00:36:07,005 --> 00:36:09,735
In the name of Allah!

358
00:36:28,885 --> 00:36:30,455
Allah is the healer!

359
00:36:31,885 --> 00:36:37,035
Send the rain of mercy on this servant
of yours.

360
00:36:38,055 --> 00:36:40,385
Grant him the remedy.

361
00:36:41,555 --> 00:36:47,255
For the sake of your prophet Muhammed
Mustafa...

362
00:36:49,235 --> 00:36:54,035
...for the sake of holy Jesus...

363
00:36:55,085 --> 00:36:58,655
...heals the wounds of this wounded
servant.

364
00:36:59,205 --> 00:37:03,605
Grant him healing, my Rabb!

365
00:37:22,705 --> 00:37:25,285
In the name of Allah!

366
00:37:25,350 --> 00:37:28,385
Bilecik Castle

367
00:37:57,485 --> 00:38:00,185
Wait, we have to search you for
precautions.

368
00:38:00,485 --> 00:38:01,805
Search them!

369
00:38:43,805 --> 00:38:45,105
You may pass.

370
00:39:31,455 --> 00:39:33,485
Where they hide is close.

371
00:39:34,255 --> 00:39:36,405
Their number is increasing.

372
00:39:37,835 --> 00:39:40,135
We will find their den.

373
00:39:51,335 --> 00:39:52,685
Come on!

374
00:40:00,435 --> 00:40:02,435
Welcome Osman bey.

375
00:40:02,935 --> 00:40:05,855
Thank you, Thank you.

376
00:40:13,035 --> 00:40:16,435
I will have a special iftar table for you.

377
00:40:17,505 --> 00:40:19,685
We'll have our wedding after the iftar.

378
00:40:19,685 --> 00:40:23,385
You can rest in your rooms if you want.

379
00:40:25,005 --> 00:40:27,135
Well thought, Justinianus.

380
00:40:28,755 --> 00:40:30,235
The road was tiring.

381
00:40:30,235 --> 00:40:32,985
You are right, Osman Bey.

382
00:40:32,985 --> 00:40:34,985
We should rest a bit.

383
00:40:36,135 --> 00:40:37,705
It's okay.

384
00:40:39,505 --> 00:40:41,535
Follow me, Osman Bey.

385
00:41:06,035 --> 00:41:08,685
Hey Masha Allah! (praise be!)

386
00:41:09,885 --> 00:41:12,055
Hey Masha Allah! (praise be!)

387
00:41:12,135 --> 00:41:14,685
This new iron mine is great!

388
00:41:20,885 --> 00:41:23,205
The weapon made of this iron
will be unbeaten!

389
00:41:23,935 --> 00:41:25,855
Our intentions are clear.

390
00:41:25,855 --> 00:41:27,855
So Allah makes it all easy for us.

391
00:41:28,305 --> 00:41:29,985
Open your eyes widely.

392
00:41:29,985 --> 00:41:33,135
There will be no one, even birds,
that doesn't stand with us!

393
00:41:33,135 --> 00:41:35,655
Come on my valiants!
Unload it!

394
00:41:47,355 --> 00:41:49,605
Chunk it up!

395
00:41:51,955 --> 00:41:56,955
So you this is where they forge
and produce weapons.

396
00:42:06,485 --> 00:42:08,035
Their dream is great.

397
00:42:08,455 --> 00:42:10,955
But they'll grumble in the gizzard.

398
00:42:11,555 --> 00:42:14,135
Command us to destoy them, my Bey!

399
00:42:14,135 --> 00:42:16,135
Not now, Husamettin.

400
00:42:16,205 --> 00:42:17,735
Not now.

401
00:42:20,505 --> 00:42:22,635
We'll let them grow up.

402
00:42:23,555 --> 00:42:25,435
The bigger they are...

403
00:42:26,585 --> 00:42:28,905
...the noiser their destruction is.

404
00:42:35,255 --> 00:42:36,755
First of all...

405
00:42:37,935 --> 00:42:39,735
I'll talk to Beys.

406
00:42:40,635 --> 00:42:42,505
I'll make sure they are loyal.

407
00:42:45,405 --> 00:42:47,605
We are going back to the tribe.

408
00:43:06,255 --> 00:43:09,535
Wait here.
Keep your eyes open just in case.

409
00:43:09,705 --> 00:43:11,705
Yes!

410
00:43:44,785 --> 00:43:46,555
Where are you headed?

411
00:43:46,835 --> 00:43:48,535
To the Red Apple.

412
00:43:52,335 --> 00:43:53,705
Son.

413
00:43:57,055 --> 00:43:59,135
My valiant son.

414
00:43:59,755 --> 00:44:01,785
I missed you a lot.

415
00:44:06,905 --> 00:44:08,955
I missed you very much, father.

416
00:44:15,085 --> 00:44:16,805
This is Osman Bey's order.

417
00:44:17,235 --> 00:44:20,005
Alp Temur is on duty.

418
00:44:21,085 --> 00:44:23,455
Ayse, does she know that?

419
00:44:29,585 --> 00:44:32,855
I have not been to myself since Fatma
went to the tableland.

420
00:44:33,305 --> 00:44:35,805
How did you manage to wait for years,
Gunduz Bey?

421
00:44:37,855 --> 00:44:40,385
Being the state requires devotion.

422
00:44:41,785 --> 00:44:43,855
Masha Allah (Praise be).

423
00:44:45,955 --> 00:44:47,805
Masha Allah (Praise be) to my son.

424
00:44:49,205 --> 00:44:51,705
We thought you were still a child.

425
00:44:51,705 --> 00:44:54,205
You are already ready to fight, valiant.

426
00:44:57,655 --> 00:45:00,235
Temur, tell us.

427
00:45:00,235 --> 00:45:03,285
Where are the kids?
Do you know where they are?

428
00:45:05,355 --> 00:45:07,135
They are locked in the dungeon.

429
00:45:12,305 --> 00:45:14,135
It shows the dungeon's location.

430
00:45:14,755 --> 00:45:17,635
I'll come again, but now I have to leave.

431
00:45:17,635 --> 00:45:19,635
I'll let you know if I learn anything.

432
00:45:19,635 --> 00:45:21,635
Thank you, Alp Temur.

433
00:45:21,635 --> 00:45:23,635
May Allah help you.

434
00:45:24,805 --> 00:45:26,135
Father.

435
00:45:30,735 --> 00:45:32,235
Be careful.

436
00:45:45,785 --> 00:45:47,285
Hay Masha Allah (praise be).

437
00:45:48,555 --> 00:45:50,935
Like father like son.

438
00:45:51,505 --> 00:45:53,335
Eyvallah (thank you) Malhun Hatun.

439
00:45:56,735 --> 00:45:58,445
It's like he said.

440
00:45:59,015 --> 00:46:02,215
We know where the dungeon is.
Now listen to me carefully.

441
00:46:13,385 --> 00:46:15,945
We'll get rid of the chain, brother.

442
00:46:17,085 --> 00:46:20,605
How are we going to do this?
Look at it, it's so tough.

443
00:46:25,205 --> 00:46:26,835
We'll find a way.

444
00:46:27,975 --> 00:46:32,905
If we can't break the chain,
we can grab the keys.

445
00:46:35,605 --> 00:46:38,985
Osman Bey must be coming to
save us.

446
00:46:42,625 --> 00:46:45,175
Say what you have to say, Alaeddin.

447
00:46:45,715 --> 00:46:47,635
I think we should wait for him, brother.

448
00:46:49,745 --> 00:46:51,325
I knew you'd say that.

449
00:46:53,125 --> 00:46:55,175
You choose waiting when it's hard.

450
00:46:56,345 --> 00:46:59,555
What can we do, brother?
What do you want me to do?

451
00:47:11,005 --> 00:47:13,085
Let's give it a try, brother.

452
00:47:13,685 --> 00:47:16,255
We'll break it if we can loose it,
Inshallah.

453
00:47:20,285 --> 00:47:21,635
Okay brother.

454
00:47:25,295 --> 00:47:28,685
One, two, tree...

455
00:47:28,975 --> 00:47:30,475
Ya Haqq!

456
00:47:32,005 --> 00:47:34,835
One, two, tree...

457
00:47:34,985 --> 00:47:36,265
Ya Haqq!

458
00:47:39,575 --> 00:47:42,455
One, two, tree...

459
00:47:42,755 --> 00:47:44,305
Ya Haqq!

460
00:48:22,615 --> 00:48:24,475
Check that out!

461
00:48:29,055 --> 00:48:30,935
You'll burn!

462
00:49:06,015 --> 00:49:08,035
You put a lot of effort.

463
00:49:08,135 --> 00:49:11,635
And a lot of gold.
It's all worth it though, Osman Bey.

464
00:49:31,645 --> 00:49:32,975
Here.

465
00:49:57,925 --> 00:49:59,315
Herd of cowards!

466
00:49:59,625 --> 00:50:03,805
It's been many years, they are still
not brave enough to face us!

467
00:50:04,435 --> 00:50:08,505
They can't stand against us. They can only
threaten us with the lives of our children.

468
00:50:09,905 --> 00:50:13,465
We are not going to let those cruels
have our kids, no matter what happens!

469
00:50:13,525 --> 00:50:17,405
Don't worry, Hatuns. They are
the grandchildren of Ertugrul Ghazi.

470
00:50:18,005 --> 00:50:20,575
They'll figure something out.

471
00:50:22,075 --> 00:50:25,545
We entered the castle.
It's haram for us to leave without them!

472
00:50:27,645 --> 00:50:29,735
May our fight be blessed!

473
00:50:29,755 --> 00:50:31,125
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

474
00:50:36,845 --> 00:50:38,565
One is approaching.

475
00:51:01,495 --> 00:51:04,535
- Gunduz Bey.
- Cerkutay!

476
00:51:09,095 --> 00:51:13,275
We came to finish a cruel,
almost ended up finishing you.

477
00:51:32,705 --> 00:51:34,235
The show shall begin.

478
00:51:41,215 --> 00:51:45,495
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

479
00:51:45,525 --> 00:51:48,975
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

480
00:51:49,015 --> 00:51:52,125
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

481
00:51:52,235 --> 00:51:55,565
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

482
00:51:55,615 --> 00:51:57,765
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

483
00:52:06,775 --> 00:52:09,015
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

484
00:52:09,045 --> 00:52:12,255
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

485
00:52:12,335 --> 00:52:15,575
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

486
00:52:15,605 --> 00:52:17,865
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

487
00:52:30,215 --> 00:52:32,055
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

488
00:52:33,785 --> 00:52:38,505
His nickname is Ceaser.
He has never been beaten.

489
00:52:41,605 --> 00:52:44,475
I am glad to have him on our side.

490
00:52:44,525 --> 00:52:47,045
What if he was our enemy?

491
00:53:04,635 --> 00:53:07,165
Masha Allah, (praise be)
He fights well.

492
00:53:07,195 --> 00:53:10,535
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

493
00:53:10,635 --> 00:53:12,755
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

494
00:53:14,345 --> 00:53:21,265
However, we never say to anyone that
"what if he was our enemy?"

495
00:53:22,595 --> 00:53:25,755
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

496
00:53:25,855 --> 00:53:29,015
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

497
00:53:34,395 --> 00:53:35,905
Alps.

498
00:53:37,335 --> 00:53:39,565
Tell me.

499
00:53:41,605 --> 00:53:44,375
Anyone want to confront Caesar?

500
00:53:45,595 --> 00:53:47,405
I can go my Bey.

501
00:53:51,325 --> 00:53:52,655
Gence Bey.

502
00:53:55,825 --> 00:53:58,545
He can't even take a punch of mine.

503
00:53:58,665 --> 00:54:01,555
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

504
00:54:01,895 --> 00:54:05,455
I'll confront him, my Bey.

505
00:54:07,835 --> 00:54:09,385
Samil!

506
00:54:11,145 --> 00:54:12,855
Tell me.

507
00:54:13,395 --> 00:54:16,445
Do you want to fight Caesar?

508
00:54:16,695 --> 00:54:20,035
I have come all the way to fight.

509
00:54:20,115 --> 00:54:23,355
Not one,
I'll fight one thousand Caesars my Bey!

510
00:54:23,425 --> 00:54:24,705
Eyvallah.

511
00:54:25,765 --> 00:54:27,905
- Turhan?
- My Bey?

512
00:54:29,275 --> 00:54:33,495
My breast is hotter than
the Blacksmith's iron. I am ready my Bey.

513
00:54:36,395 --> 00:54:41,985
But I want Abdurrahim to fight.

514
00:55:00,295 --> 00:55:01,865
Sisters!

515
00:55:09,615 --> 00:55:11,325
No one is around.

516
00:55:15,125 --> 00:55:16,665
Be careful.

517
00:55:22,455 --> 00:55:24,975
Ah, my belly!
I can't wait more!

518
00:55:25,145 --> 00:55:27,175
Ah! Ah!

519
00:55:27,175 --> 00:55:28,765
What are you doing here?

520
00:55:28,825 --> 00:55:31,125
You should be in your rooms
until the supper.

521
00:55:31,155 --> 00:55:33,665
We need a doctor!
A doctor! My belly hurts!

522
00:55:34,495 --> 00:55:36,065
Ah! Ah!

523
00:55:36,975 --> 00:55:40,515
What are you looking at?
Hatun is fighting for his life!

524
00:55:40,695 --> 00:55:44,225
Is this how you host your guests?
We need a doctor!

525
00:55:45,335 --> 00:55:49,035
Okay. Go to your room.
We'll get a doctor.

526
00:55:49,045 --> 00:55:52,745
We have no time to wait!
We'll go by ourselves.

527
00:55:53,025 --> 00:55:56,275
Go to your rooms now.
We'll get you a doctor.

528
00:55:56,465 --> 00:55:58,315
What's happening?

529
00:56:00,985 --> 00:56:03,055
They want a doctor, sir.

530
00:56:06,955 --> 00:56:09,495
Go back to your duty.
I'll take care of it.

531
00:56:21,885 --> 00:56:24,435
Hay Masha Allah, my valiant.
You came just in time!

532
00:56:25,695 --> 00:56:29,755
The cellar is at the end of the corridor.
It's time for shift change.

533
00:56:29,755 --> 00:56:31,995
There'll be two guards.
Be careful.

534
00:56:33,325 --> 00:56:37,145
Son you be careful too, okay?

535
00:56:37,955 --> 00:56:40,265
Let's go Hatuns.

536
00:57:09,685 --> 00:57:12,555
Thank my Lord.

537
00:57:14,105 --> 00:57:15,635
He opened his eyes.

538
00:57:19,505 --> 00:57:21,085
Kossess?

539
00:57:21,865 --> 00:57:24,895
How are you?
Are you better?

540
00:57:30,005 --> 00:57:31,795
Sheik Edebali.

541
00:57:33,545 --> 00:57:35,085
Thank you.

542
00:57:37,445 --> 00:57:38,965
Osman.

543
00:57:40,585 --> 00:57:42,325
I and Osman...

544
00:57:44,035 --> 00:57:48,535
Kids, Orhan, Alaeddin.

545
00:57:48,725 --> 00:57:50,805
Did Osman save them?

546
00:57:51,225 --> 00:57:53,445
Eesy, Kosses, easy.

547
00:57:55,415 --> 00:57:59,195
Your wounds haven't healed yet.
Move slowly.

548
00:58:01,995 --> 00:58:03,995
Did he save the kids?

549
00:58:05,315 --> 00:58:08,205
Osman is at Bilecik Castle now.

550
00:58:08,775 --> 00:58:12,545
He'll get our shahzades back
in here safe and sound, Inshallah.

551
00:58:16,845 --> 00:58:20,375
Sheik Edebali...
I know...

552
00:58:21,195 --> 00:58:23,775
You don't have great reaction
to things.

553
00:58:24,395 --> 00:58:26,975
But I am still surprised to see you
so calm...

554
00:58:28,615 --> 00:58:32,395
...when your grandchildren are abducted.

555
00:58:33,955 --> 00:58:37,495
How can I reject what comes from Allah,
Kosses?

556
00:58:38,065 --> 00:58:43,645
It seems like evil, but there
may be wisdom and goodness hidden inside.

557
00:58:45,245 --> 00:58:49,255
I entrusted my shahzades to Allah.

558
00:58:49,965 --> 00:58:54,475
Osman Bey and their mothers
took precautions and went for them.

559
00:58:55,295 --> 00:58:59,795
They'll come back with
Orhan and Alaeddin Inshallah.

560
00:59:00,215 --> 00:59:02,265
Inshallah.

561
00:59:05,405 --> 00:59:07,905
I could never stay calm like that.

562
00:59:08,735 --> 00:59:14,695
Thank Allah, both our heart and our
beloved ones are entrusted to Allah.

563
00:59:16,445 --> 00:59:20,135
What we need to do is to
pray with patience.

564
00:59:21,255 --> 00:59:23,285
Sorry to trouble you.

565
00:59:24,375 --> 00:59:27,605
You took care of me among
all those troubles.

566
00:59:28,105 --> 00:59:33,025
Nothing is trouble about taking care
of the life that Allah has given, Kosses.

567
00:59:35,415 --> 00:59:41,275
It wouldn't mean anything if we left
you with your wounds...

568
00:59:41,275 --> 00:59:44,225
...and start grieving for our shahzades.

569
00:59:48,405 --> 00:59:50,465
I am not from your religion.

570
00:59:52,965 --> 00:59:55,745
But I am lucky to be your friend.

571
00:59:56,805 --> 00:59:58,735
I appreciate it, Sheik Edebali.

572
01:00:01,005 --> 01:00:04,005
Be a friend, or an enemy.

573
01:00:05,915 --> 01:00:08,975
Be a Muslim, or not...

574
01:00:11,075 --> 01:00:16,875
If you are hungry, oppressed or wounded
in the land of Muslims...

575
01:00:17,025 --> 01:00:21,615
...that Muslim will find cure
as he heals you.

576
01:00:23,765 --> 01:00:26,315
It doesn't matter if you share
the same religion or not.

577
01:00:27,725 --> 01:00:32,475
Mercy is what's left us from
the messenger of Allah.

578
01:00:33,045 --> 01:00:35,115
Peace be upon him.

579
01:00:37,145 --> 01:00:39,145
The compasssionate Allah...

580
01:00:39,155 --> 01:00:45,075
put the blue sky and brave ground
in the service of the whole humanity.

581
01:00:45,595 --> 01:00:51,335
What we need to do is to show mercy
for whoever needs it.

582
01:00:54,005 --> 01:00:57,005
Our fight against the cruel...

583
01:00:58,285 --> 01:01:00,715
...and our opposition against the devil...

584
01:01:02,235 --> 01:01:04,505
...comes from
our compassion for the innocents.

585
01:01:08,445 --> 01:01:11,225
-Eyvallah.
-Eyvallah.

586
01:01:16,813 --> 01:01:17,933
Abdurrahim.

587
01:01:18,365 --> 01:01:20,855
Go show what you got.

588
01:01:21,985 --> 01:01:23,375
As you command, my Bey.

589
01:01:24,535 --> 01:02:09,035
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

590
01:02:10,565 --> 01:02:44,135
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

591
01:02:48,335 --> 01:02:50,655
It's dangerous when the
armor is off, Osman Bey.

592
01:02:51,545 --> 01:02:52,845
If you want to...

593
01:02:53,025 --> 01:02:56,745
No.
Armor makes us heavy.

594
01:02:58,255 --> 01:03:00,565
Continue.
Come on!

595
01:03:03,915 --> 01:03:20,505
Caesar! Caesar! Caesar!

596
01:03:20,575 --> 01:03:23,835
Boo! Boo!

597
01:03:23,965 --> 01:03:28,185
Boo! Boo!

598
01:03:28,365 --> 01:03:30,315
Get up!

599
01:03:30,935 --> 01:03:33,515
Boo! Boo!

600
01:03:34,275 --> 01:03:43,305
Boo! Boo!

601
01:03:43,345 --> 01:03:46,645
Caesar couldn't take care of Abdurrahim,
Justinianus.

602
01:03:49,135 --> 01:03:51,685
Summon a couple more soldiers...

603
01:03:52,655 --> 01:03:54,465
And make it fair.

604
01:03:54,475 --> 01:03:55,845
It's okay for me.

605
01:03:56,555 --> 01:03:58,145
Soldiers!

606
01:03:58,235 --> 01:04:01,025
Show our friends how hospitable we are!

607
01:04:03,765 --> 01:04:07,085
Hit! Hit! Hit!

608
01:04:08,515 --> 01:04:10,775
No way, we'll fight too, Gence Bey.

609
01:04:10,885 --> 01:04:13,445
- Lucky for us.
- Stop, valiants.

610
01:04:13,445 --> 01:04:14,705
My Bey asked me.

611
01:04:16,225 --> 01:04:18,225
Abdurrahim is enough.

612
01:04:18,445 --> 01:04:20,295
Let's watch.

613
01:04:20,295 --> 01:04:44,385
Hit! Hit! Hit!

614
01:04:45,705 --> 01:04:56,725
Hit! Hit! Hit!

615
01:05:00,755 --> 01:05:17,325
Hit! Hit! Hit!

616
01:05:29,895 --> 01:05:36,385
Get up! Get up!

617
01:05:36,385 --> 01:05:38,675
Kill him!

618
01:05:41,185 --> 01:05:42,945
It was a fair fight.

619
01:05:43,165 --> 01:05:45,045
Your men fought well.

620
01:05:45,565 --> 01:05:50,395
But Abdurrahim cannot be beaten.

621
01:05:53,095 --> 01:05:54,885
Thanks, Osman Bey.

622
01:06:50,275 --> 01:06:51,575
My Bey!

623
01:06:53,745 --> 01:06:55,835
Kids are in the dungeon.

624
01:06:58,435 --> 01:07:00,985
Bala Hatun is around them.

625
01:07:02,585 --> 01:07:05,085
We are waiting for your command.

626
01:07:08,625 --> 01:07:10,715
We are waiting for iftar.

627
01:07:31,195 --> 01:07:35,095
We are with you at iftar.
What did you cook for us?

628
01:07:35,095 --> 01:07:37,605
I have unbelievable meals for you.

629
01:07:38,345 --> 01:07:39,705
Is that so?

630
01:07:41,805 --> 01:07:43,375
Eyvallah.

631
01:07:49,005 --> 01:07:50,575
Eyvallah.

632
01:07:57,115 --> 01:07:59,645
Bilecik Castle.

633
01:08:13,385 --> 01:08:17,215
- I have no power left.
- Hang on.

634
01:08:24,904 --> 01:08:27,715
You carry Ertugrul Ghazi's blood, brother!

635
01:08:27,984 --> 01:08:29,564
Don't give up.

636
01:08:31,175 --> 01:08:32,725
Come on, one more time.

637
01:08:33,755 --> 01:08:38,335
One, two, three...
Ya Haqq!

638
01:08:44,225 --> 01:08:48,814
One, two, three...
Ya Haqq!

639
01:09:01,515 --> 01:09:03,604
They are moving, brother.

640
01:09:03,955 --> 01:09:06,955
We have to do what we have to do now.

641
01:09:07,455 --> 01:09:09,675
Come on brother, let's do it.

642
01:09:11,814 --> 01:09:16,835
One, two, three...
Ya Haqq!

643
01:09:21,255 --> 01:09:26,325
One, two, three...
Ya Haqq!

644
01:09:36,085 --> 01:09:38,849
KIZILBEYOGLU TRIBE

645
01:09:39,385 --> 01:09:46,125
Martados informed that Osman Bey is going
to be murdered tonight in Bilecik Castle.

646
01:09:48,075 --> 01:09:49,635
Murdered?

647
01:09:51,825 --> 01:09:54,635
We have to tell people and
unite, Barkin Bey.

648
01:09:54,655 --> 01:09:56,735
We have to depart to Bilecik.

649
01:09:56,805 --> 01:09:58,835
We can't leave Osman Bey alone.

650
01:09:58,875 --> 01:10:01,065
Do you think that
I didn't think of it?

651
01:10:03,435 --> 01:10:05,465
I sent my alps to Kayi tribe immediately.

652
01:10:05,805 --> 01:10:07,885
They'll go to Bilecik from there.

653
01:10:08,905 --> 01:10:10,675
I did what I needed to.

654
01:10:11,495 --> 01:10:14,005
But anything can happen.

655
01:10:14,085 --> 01:10:18,235
The ones who want to kill Osman Bey
won't leave Sogut alone.

656
01:10:19,255 --> 01:10:21,095
Sogut is Turk's land!

657
01:10:23,035 --> 01:10:26,255
We are not to leave there without a leader.

658
01:10:26,895 --> 01:10:31,445
Therefore, I will manage Sogut.

659
01:10:34,565 --> 01:10:36,565
Barkin Bey is not right.

660
01:10:38,055 --> 01:10:40,215
This is disobeying Osman Bey.

661
01:10:41,075 --> 01:10:42,805
I don't accept it.

662
01:10:43,015 --> 01:10:45,545
I am okay with helping Sogut but...

663
01:10:45,545 --> 01:10:48,115
claiming the authority is not acceptable.

664
01:10:48,115 --> 01:10:52,835
Beys! Osman Bey is closer to me than
he is to any of you!

665
01:10:53,525 --> 01:10:59,525
I prefer managing Sogut to
losing my land!

666
01:11:02,045 --> 01:11:05,465
Headless herd is invaded by jackals!

667
01:11:11,435 --> 01:11:14,525
Now tell me.

668
01:11:15,735 --> 01:11:19,815
Are we going to let Turk's flag down
because Osman Bey is not around?

669
01:11:20,955 --> 01:11:25,145
Someone has to raise that flag.

670
01:11:43,855 --> 01:11:45,705
Barkin what are you doing?

671
01:11:45,705 --> 01:11:48,255
You lied to Beys!
You didn't sent alps to the tribe.

672
01:11:48,255 --> 01:11:50,255
There's no explanation of this!

673
01:11:50,845 --> 01:11:52,435
Hatun.

674
01:11:53,075 --> 01:11:59,365
I had to do it to protect
the legacy of your father and uncle.

675
01:12:03,505 --> 01:12:06,735
I cannot let the infidels decide on
the fate of our community...

676
01:12:07,755 --> 01:12:12,075
...just because of Osman Bey's conceit.

677
01:12:21,385 --> 01:12:24,919
Bilecik Castle

678
01:12:38,835 --> 01:12:41,335
I guess this is time for you to eat.

679
01:12:44,415 --> 01:12:48,205
Eyvallah.
It's iftar time.

680
01:13:39,255 --> 01:13:41,085
Thank Allah.

681
01:13:49,585 --> 01:13:51,935
When are we going to act, sir?

682
01:13:51,995 --> 01:13:54,505
We are waiting for all of them,
don't hurry.

683
01:14:15,845 --> 01:14:17,235
Come on.

684
01:14:41,775 --> 01:14:44,095
Damn it!
They run away!

685
01:14:44,095 --> 01:14:45,955
Search the castle!

686
01:15:11,605 --> 01:15:13,445
You!
Where are you going?

687
01:15:18,255 --> 01:15:19,755
Bala Hatun.

688
01:15:20,075 --> 01:15:22,625
Go to the cellar to get the weapons.

689
01:15:22,705 --> 01:15:24,055
Go.

690
01:15:24,115 --> 01:15:25,955
Let's go Hatuns.

691
01:15:32,785 --> 01:15:34,835
What are you doing here?

692
01:15:37,725 --> 01:15:39,565
We found what we were looking for.

693
01:15:39,755 --> 01:15:41,085
Come on.

694
01:15:56,285 --> 01:15:59,465
I'd love to cut them with my double sword.

695
01:16:00,955 --> 01:16:03,125
I'll have to be satisfied with this one.

696
01:16:03,855 --> 01:16:05,635
Let's go Cerkutay.

697
01:16:06,335 --> 01:16:07,635
You!

698
01:16:23,965 --> 01:16:26,315
We found it, thank Allah!
Come on.

699
01:16:40,045 --> 01:16:41,405
Hatuns!

700
01:16:41,405 --> 01:16:44,655
We have to break the fast,
even when there's a war.

701
01:16:45,115 --> 01:16:49,135
Our mouth is free now.
Here you go.

702
01:16:49,195 --> 01:16:50,555
Come on.
In the name of Allah.

703
01:17:02,345 --> 01:17:03,465
Amen.

704
01:17:29,035 --> 01:17:30,335
Let's go.

705
01:17:31,735 --> 01:17:33,275
Sisters.

706
01:17:37,845 --> 01:17:40,435
Open the door!

707
01:17:42,115 --> 01:17:44,695
Hey insiders!
Open the door!

708
01:17:44,695 --> 01:17:46,495
Open it!

709
01:17:46,495 --> 01:17:48,575
Soldiers pop up everywhere!

710
01:17:48,575 --> 01:17:51,655
They must have borrowed all the
soldiers from other Lords!

711
01:17:51,755 --> 01:17:53,815
Cowards!
They can gather whoever they want.

712
01:17:53,815 --> 01:17:56,725
We'll overcome with Osman Bey's plan.

713
01:17:58,145 --> 01:17:59,955
Open the door!

714
01:18:09,445 --> 01:18:13,315
Open the door!
Open the door!

715
01:18:17,375 --> 01:18:19,385
Empower us my Allah!

716
01:18:20,635 --> 01:18:22,215
Open the door!

717
01:18:44,625 --> 01:18:48,645
Master Davut would know how to get rid
of this if he were here.

718
01:18:50,675 --> 01:18:52,795
Brother, come on.

719
01:18:54,435 --> 01:18:56,625
The chain is about to loose.

720
01:18:58,015 --> 01:19:00,575
- We'll get out of here.
- We will, brother.

721
01:19:04,005 --> 01:19:09,075
One, two, three...
Ya Haqq!

722
01:19:29,675 --> 01:19:32,735
Sir, the wedding procession is about to
enter Bilecik.

723
01:19:44,125 --> 01:19:46,425
Congratulations, Justinianus.

724
01:19:46,985 --> 01:19:48,525
Congratulations.

725
01:20:05,285 --> 01:20:08,049
Inegol Castle

726
01:20:12,355 --> 01:20:16,895
My caravans has passed here for years.

727
01:20:17,095 --> 01:20:19,825
I put my men on their tail
tens of times.

728
01:20:20,125 --> 01:20:22,365
I followed them, but...

729
01:20:23,285 --> 01:20:24,845
I couldn't find them.

730
01:20:27,235 --> 01:20:34,295
It is really, really strange that
they built their headquarters there.

731
01:20:36,485 --> 01:20:42,845
As he is going to die tonight,
he does not pose danger.

732
01:20:45,115 --> 01:20:46,695
I'll ruin...

733
01:20:47,685 --> 01:20:50,825
...their headquarters first.

734
01:20:53,185 --> 01:21:00,785
Then I will burn all their catapults
that they made to demolish my walls.

735
01:21:02,735 --> 01:21:04,625
And..

736
01:21:07,735 --> 01:21:09,815
...my mine!

737
01:21:11,415 --> 01:21:13,655
You lost your mine...

738
01:21:13,985 --> 01:21:18,775
...but you'll regain it now.

739
01:21:27,995 --> 01:21:30,535
Sir, we are ready to attack.

740
01:21:43,825 --> 01:21:51,045
These lands will enlighten with
the fire we light.

741
01:22:21,750 --> 01:22:25,260
What am I going to do now?
What will happen to me?

742
01:22:28,950 --> 01:22:31,000
Don't cry, beautiful daughter.

743
01:22:31,550 --> 01:22:32,850
Uh, don't cry.

744
01:22:35,385 --> 01:22:40,945
Osman Bey saved you from those ignobles,
just like how you wanted.

745
01:22:41,035 --> 01:22:44,085
Now he'll send you to your aunt.

746
01:22:44,205 --> 01:22:46,025
Don't be afraid, my beautiful daughter.

747
01:22:46,095 --> 01:22:49,125
You are decent people.
I appreciate you.

748
01:22:54,215 --> 01:22:56,595
Mother, are you okay?

749
01:22:56,975 --> 01:22:58,735
Your color faded!

750
01:22:58,925 --> 01:23:02,115
Zehra, run!
Bring water! Mother!

751
01:23:03,385 --> 01:23:05,525
I am fine, daughter.

752
01:23:14,585 --> 01:23:16,915
This is how it is to be old.

753
01:23:17,455 --> 01:23:19,535
I can't catch my breath time to time.

754
01:23:22,185 --> 01:23:26,675
Zehra, take Holofira to the tent.

755
01:23:27,325 --> 01:23:30,085
Let her sleep and rest.

756
01:23:31,165 --> 01:23:32,875
I will, mother.

757
01:23:42,505 --> 01:23:44,885
You are not well.

758
01:23:45,015 --> 01:23:47,045
We should see a healer.

759
01:23:47,235 --> 01:23:48,805
Ayse.

760
01:23:50,135 --> 01:23:52,075
I know my time is coming.

761
01:23:52,375 --> 01:23:54,275
Mother, what are you talking about?!

762
01:23:54,485 --> 01:23:57,865
- I'll see Kumral Abdal.
- Sit down, daugter.

763
01:23:58,085 --> 01:23:59,385
Sit down.

764
01:23:59,975 --> 01:24:02,545
I did what I could do.

765
01:24:03,085 --> 01:24:05,675
The rest is Allah's command.

766
01:24:06,935 --> 01:24:15,475
My wish is to live long enough to see
Osman and my sons return.

767
01:24:16,695 --> 01:24:19,375
We waited for
this victory too long, daughter.

768
01:24:19,535 --> 01:24:21,645
Mother, my beautiful daughter.

769
01:24:22,025 --> 01:24:24,735
Don't talk like that, please.

770
01:24:24,925 --> 01:24:29,685
Dying before Osman returns with victory
is not appropriate for me.

771
01:24:31,005 --> 01:24:33,255
Listen to me very well now.

772
01:24:34,015 --> 01:24:36,555
If I can't make it...

773
01:24:37,935 --> 01:24:40,525
There are packs in the chest.

774
01:24:43,345 --> 01:24:46,615
Give them to my grandchildren.

775
01:24:46,775 --> 01:24:48,055
Mother.

776
01:24:51,165 --> 01:24:52,485
Mother.

777
01:25:09,015 --> 01:25:11,425
Hay Masha Allah Hatuns.

778
01:25:13,855 --> 01:25:15,925
Hay Masha Allah (praise be)

779
01:25:16,995 --> 01:25:21,105
They want to burn us in this caslte.
Let's ruin their game!

780
01:25:22,545 --> 01:25:23,895
But...

781
01:25:24,975 --> 01:25:28,495
I don't like fighting with
the infidel's sword at all.

782
01:25:37,855 --> 01:25:40,175
It's a relic.

783
01:25:41,345 --> 01:25:44,755
I go down but my swords don't.

784
01:25:45,075 --> 01:25:49,595
They need to cut my arms to
take these swords from me.

785
01:25:50,455 --> 01:25:53,215
A sword lives longer than Adam, Cerkutay.

786
01:25:54,515 --> 01:25:58,085
Bamsi Bey's swords witnessed many wars.

787
01:25:58,815 --> 01:26:02,145
Masha Allah, you take care of his relics
very well.

788
01:26:02,525 --> 01:26:04,065
I do, right?

789
01:26:04,225 --> 01:26:06,125
You glorify it.

790
01:26:07,045 --> 01:26:09,935
Bilecik soldiers will hand us the castle
without fighting...

791
01:26:10,155 --> 01:26:12,755
...when they see how eager you are
for the war.

792
01:26:14,215 --> 01:26:18,055
- I was a good warrior, Gunduz Bey.
- I know, Cerkutay.

793
01:26:18,725 --> 01:26:22,785
But I learned the process of war
from you.

794
01:26:25,385 --> 01:26:27,605
The right way is tough.

795
01:26:28,955 --> 01:26:31,065
There is shahada.

796
01:26:31,685 --> 01:26:34,065
I thought Cerkutay wouldn't die.

797
01:26:36,615 --> 01:26:40,885
A sword lives longer than Adam, Gunduz Bey.

798
01:26:42,345 --> 01:26:45,875
I will hand these relics on my son Kayi.

799
01:26:47,895 --> 01:26:52,915
You become soil, I become soil,
Conquerers die...

800
01:26:53,055 --> 01:26:57,625
...but the conquests will remain
as a legacy for generations.

801
01:26:58,735 --> 01:27:03,245
Our dawah is
longer than our lives, Cerkutay. Let's go.

802
01:27:05,985 --> 01:27:10,575
The more infidels we kill the better
until we die.

803
01:27:11,945 --> 01:27:14,075
Our fight shall be blessed!

804
01:27:14,245 --> 01:27:16,105
Let's go.

805
01:27:16,455 --> 01:27:18,275
Let's go sisters.

806
01:28:35,535 --> 01:28:37,125
Trap!

807
01:28:43,805 --> 01:28:46,325
This was your last betrayal.

808
01:28:52,765 --> 01:28:55,275
You shouldn't have done this, Osman!

809
01:28:55,605 --> 01:28:58,635
Where will you run in your own castle?

810
01:29:03,775 --> 01:29:08,345
Allah is eternal!

811
01:29:48,515 --> 01:29:50,705
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

812
01:29:54,445 --> 01:29:57,125
Let's go, sisters!

813
01:31:04,005 --> 01:31:05,295
Infidels!

814
01:31:06,255 --> 01:31:08,075
You won't make it!

815
01:31:10,895 --> 01:31:14,585
My Allah, don't let the cruels!

816
01:31:23,975 --> 01:31:25,335
My Creator!

817
01:31:26,365 --> 01:31:28,595
Help my father.

818
01:31:31,445 --> 01:31:35,035
Make infidels fall in their own trap,
my Creator.

819
01:31:38,865 --> 01:31:42,005
- Amin.
- Amin.

820
01:31:53,015 --> 01:31:56,085
One, two, three!

821
01:33:28,515 --> 01:33:30,085
Cerkutay!

822
01:33:36,415 --> 01:33:41,585
My heart is on the right.

823
01:33:54,585 --> 01:33:56,125
Malhun!

824
01:33:57,725 --> 01:33:59,265
Bala!

825
01:34:02,485 --> 01:34:04,375
Are you okay?

826
01:34:15,085 --> 01:34:18,105
You will never get your children, Osman!
Never!

827
01:34:19,755 --> 01:34:21,775
Where are you going?

828
01:34:38,695 --> 01:34:41,745
Don't let anyone pass.
Be careful.

829
01:34:42,315 --> 01:34:45,065
Where are you running, Justinianus?

830
01:34:45,205 --> 01:34:47,755
I'll shed your dirty blood.

831
01:34:48,495 --> 01:34:50,645
Soldiers, attack!

832
01:34:58,695 --> 01:35:01,065
Come to me, dog herd!

833
01:35:01,275 --> 01:35:02,625
Come on.

834
01:35:14,445 --> 01:35:17,415
Come on, today is shahada day!

835
01:35:24,265 --> 01:35:25,775
Hatuns!

836
01:35:31,065 --> 01:35:32,915
The dungeon is on this way.

837
01:35:33,555 --> 01:35:36,385
This way! Hurry up!

838
01:35:37,125 --> 01:35:39,975
Cerkutay, delay them with Hatuns.

839
01:35:40,115 --> 01:35:42,175
Come on Hatuns!

840
01:35:50,175 --> 01:35:53,355
You'll drop away one by one
until we end you all.

841
01:36:18,355 --> 01:36:21,355
Your owner's end will be worse.

842
01:36:39,735 --> 01:36:41,525
Come on Hatuns!

843
01:36:42,325 --> 01:36:44,115
Let's go Bala!

844
01:37:02,255 --> 01:37:03,615
Kids!

845
01:37:05,695 --> 01:37:07,045
Kids!

846
01:37:10,795 --> 01:37:12,425
My valiants!

847
01:37:12,885 --> 01:37:14,925
Hold on my valiants!

848
01:37:34,215 --> 01:37:36,755
Ignoble Justinianus.

849
01:37:36,975 --> 01:37:38,995
What if they did something bad, Osman?

850
01:37:39,035 --> 01:37:43,485
No.
His life is dependant on my sons' lives.

851
01:37:47,195 --> 01:37:49,995
He'll use them to
get out of the castle.

852
01:37:52,245 --> 01:37:53,705
My Bey.

853
01:37:55,005 --> 01:37:57,015
They must have used the secret passage.

854
01:37:57,395 --> 01:37:59,715
- This way.
- We leave at once!

855
01:38:06,755 --> 01:38:08,555
The secret passage is on this way.

856
01:38:11,285 --> 01:38:13,515
Come on hurry up!
Get them!

857
01:38:14,035 --> 01:38:17,345
My Bey, we'll take care of them.
You go.

858
01:38:17,915 --> 01:38:20,025
Go save the kids, Osman.

859
01:38:21,555 --> 01:38:23,365
Come on Osman Bey.

860
01:38:23,765 --> 01:38:25,135
Go.

861
01:38:51,255 --> 01:38:52,645
Come on!

862
01:38:55,875 --> 01:38:58,055
My father will make you pay for this, Lord.

863
01:38:58,245 --> 01:39:00,615
Prepare your grave.

864
01:39:01,235 --> 01:39:04,285
The only thing your father will do
is to die with his sons!

865
01:39:15,885 --> 01:39:18,935
I'll hang your corpse in the square!

866
01:39:29,365 --> 01:39:30,735
Move!

867
01:39:36,085 --> 01:39:37,435
My Bey!

868
01:39:39,640 --> 01:39:42,220
I know where to go.

869
01:39:43,570 --> 01:39:45,270
Show up on their way, my Bey.

870
01:39:46,570 --> 01:39:48,340
Eyvallah Temur.

871
01:39:48,620 --> 01:39:49,920
Eyvallah.

872
01:39:53,040 --> 01:39:56,070
You are running to your death, Justinianus.

873
01:39:57,620 --> 01:39:59,670
Your time is up.

874
01:40:06,340 --> 01:40:08,170
Come on, to the horses!

875
01:40:08,420 --> 01:40:10,490
It's impossible to take this castle.

876
01:40:10,490 --> 01:40:14,240
Let's save our lives to seek revenge!

877
01:40:34,340 --> 01:40:36,340
You vile heathen!

878
01:40:36,540 --> 01:40:38,290
You are the traitor!

879
01:40:43,070 --> 01:40:47,620
Your life nor your castle...

880
01:40:48,790 --> 01:40:50,790
you will be saving neither.

881
01:40:52,370 --> 01:40:55,020
Don't come closer, Osman.
They'll both die!

882
01:40:56,570 --> 01:41:02,420
You attempted to kill my wives
and children.

883
01:41:05,920 --> 01:41:08,490
Don't, Osman.
We can come to an agreement.

884
01:41:09,320 --> 01:41:11,020
Where the words end...

885
01:41:13,640 --> 01:41:15,790
the weapon of justice speaks!

886
01:41:20,940 --> 01:41:23,340
Don't, Osman!
Don't!

887
01:41:29,520 --> 01:41:34,320
The end of all the tyrants will
be like you.

888
01:41:39,420 --> 01:41:41,390
Either by my hands...

889
01:41:41,570 --> 01:41:49,620
or by another valiant man who holds the
weapon of justice!

890
01:42:04,170 --> 01:42:05,540
My children!

891
01:42:05,540 --> 01:42:06,840
Father!

892
01:42:06,920 --> 01:42:08,670
My lion!

893
01:42:15,470 --> 01:42:17,020
Are you alright?

894
01:42:17,870 --> 01:42:19,370
I am, father.

895
01:42:19,420 --> 01:42:20,770
Mashallah.

896
01:42:20,770 --> 01:42:23,590
-What about you, Alahaddin?
-We are alright, father

897
01:42:23,590 --> 01:42:25,240
My lions!

898
01:42:25,640 --> 01:42:27,340
My lions.

899
01:42:31,140 --> 01:42:33,140
Your uncle's son, Aktemur.

900
01:42:34,120 --> 01:42:35,870
Your brother.

901
01:42:37,570 --> 01:42:39,570
My shehzads!

902
01:42:43,440 --> 01:42:44,940
Mashallah.

903
01:42:46,370 --> 01:42:48,440
Lions!

904
01:42:48,440 --> 01:42:50,440
My lions!

905
01:42:52,570 --> 01:42:53,920
Lions!

906
01:43:18,740 --> 01:43:20,490
Osman Bey is coming!

907
01:43:20,920 --> 01:43:22,770
Long live Osman Bey!

908
01:43:22,770 --> 01:43:39,340
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

909
01:43:39,470 --> 01:43:47,140
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

910
01:43:47,170 --> 01:44:27,390
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

911
01:44:29,820 --> 01:44:31,840
My children.

912
01:44:55,140 --> 01:44:56,490
You.

913
01:44:57,770 --> 01:45:00,790
Go to everyone Basilleus knows.

914
01:45:02,990 --> 01:45:10,820
And say that I ask for ransom
for the soldiers. Two chests of gold.

915
01:45:11,820 --> 01:45:13,190
Come on.

916
01:45:27,590 --> 01:45:29,440
Orhan! My valiants!

917
01:45:29,920 --> 01:45:31,270
Mother!

918
01:45:32,820 --> 01:45:34,370
My child!

919
01:45:34,370 --> 01:45:36,370
My son!

920
01:45:37,790 --> 01:45:39,820
Thank Allah!

921
01:45:54,890 --> 01:45:57,470
Thank Allah!

922
01:45:57,470 --> 01:45:58,970
Are you alright?

923
01:45:58,970 --> 01:46:00,740
I'm alright, mother.

924
01:46:00,740 --> 01:46:03,290
Orhan! My Orhan!

925
01:46:12,520 --> 01:46:14,290
Are you alright?

926
01:46:14,290 --> 01:46:16,140
You are fine, right?

927
01:46:20,190 --> 01:46:22,070
Thank you, my bey.

928
01:46:27,370 --> 01:46:28,920
Mashallah.

929
01:46:29,790 --> 01:46:31,340
Mashallah.

930
01:46:57,270 --> 01:47:00,020
Take them all to the dungeon.

931
01:47:02,670 --> 01:47:04,240
Come on.

932
01:47:20,690 --> 01:47:22,770
Thank Allah, my bey.

933
01:47:22,820 --> 01:47:24,570
Thank Allah.

934
01:47:39,885 --> 01:47:42,894
Kızılbeyoğlu Tribe

935
01:47:59,515 --> 01:48:01,515
May I enter, Barkın Bey.

936
01:48:01,515 --> 01:48:02,895
Come in.

937
01:48:12,785 --> 01:48:14,585
Speak, beys.

938
01:48:15,065 --> 01:48:17,635
What brings you here.

939
01:48:17,635 --> 01:48:19,635
We are against you taking Söğüt.

940
01:48:19,865 --> 01:48:21,935
If you attempt this...

941
01:48:22,035 --> 01:48:26,615
our alps won't restrain from
killing you.

942
01:48:34,935 --> 01:48:38,515
I told you why I'm doing it.

943
01:48:43,435 --> 01:48:45,965
But you didn't understand it.

944
01:49:08,815 --> 01:49:12,015
Then, I was lying.

945
01:49:14,115 --> 01:49:15,915
Now, I'll speak the truth.

946
01:49:19,085 --> 01:49:22,615
Osman will die!
I'll have Söğüt!

947
01:49:25,185 --> 01:49:27,435
It'll be mine!

948
01:49:30,840 --> 01:49:32,890
May I enter, my bey?

949
01:49:32,910 --> 01:49:34,290
Come in.

950
01:49:42,150 --> 01:49:45,020
My bey, he is waiting for you.

951
01:49:59,670 --> 01:50:02,220
Bury them without getting seen.

952
01:50:32,150 --> 01:50:33,900
Salam Alaikum.

953
01:50:55,500 --> 01:50:57,530
Allah Almighty speaks the truth.

954
01:51:00,080 --> 01:51:02,100
Alaikum Salam, Akça.

955
01:51:02,300 --> 01:51:03,880
Come.

956
01:51:05,550 --> 01:51:07,630
It's for the sahur time, my sheik.

957
01:51:11,230 --> 01:51:16,230
It's apparent that you didn't just come
to bring me my sahur meal, Akça.

958
01:51:17,800 --> 01:51:20,680
Speak what your heart has.

959
01:51:26,350 --> 01:51:27,880
Thank Allah.

960
01:51:29,680 --> 01:51:35,000
Bilecik Castle is a battlefield
since this evening, my sheik.

961
01:51:36,550 --> 01:51:38,550
Do we have information?

962
01:51:39,800 --> 01:51:42,380
Our brothers sent the news, my sheik.

963
01:51:44,330 --> 01:51:48,850
Osman Bey triumphed in Bilecik Castle.

964
01:51:54,250 --> 01:51:56,830
Thank Allah for this victory.

965
01:52:06,080 --> 01:52:10,600
Take care of our visitor Kosses.

966
01:52:11,280 --> 01:52:13,050
Provide everything he needs.

967
01:52:13,300 --> 01:52:14,630
And...

968
01:52:15,580 --> 01:52:19,430
our guest also get the benefit
from Qur-an.

969
01:52:20,950 --> 01:52:24,230
If he wishes, someone should
read him Qur-an.

970
01:52:25,380 --> 01:52:27,050
As you say, my sheik.

971
01:52:27,430 --> 01:52:29,000
Thank you.

972
01:52:38,185 --> 01:52:40,685
That will never do!

973
01:52:47,635 --> 01:52:52,205
One who can't control his anger
is destined to lose, Nikola.

974
01:52:52,755 --> 01:52:56,335
Being powerful is directing your anger
at your enemies.

975
01:52:57,035 --> 01:52:58,835
Not at yourself.

976
01:52:59,135 --> 01:53:00,935
This was the last.

977
01:53:03,835 --> 01:53:05,585
This was the last.

978
01:53:06,635 --> 01:53:08,405
This was the last.

979
01:53:08,405 --> 01:53:10,205
Be patient, Nikola.

980
01:53:10,205 --> 01:53:11,435
Be patient.

981
01:53:11,435 --> 01:53:13,435
Should I be patient, Master Darius?

982
01:53:13,435 --> 01:53:16,485
What else did I do all this time?

983
01:53:16,485 --> 01:53:17,855
I'm being patient.

984
01:53:17,855 --> 01:53:20,855
Isn't it time to get the fruit?

985
01:53:20,855 --> 01:53:25,785
Destroying the ammunition Osman
gathered to conquer İnegöl...

986
01:53:25,785 --> 01:53:29,155
will be a beautiful fruit
from your patience, Nikola.

987
01:53:29,305 --> 01:53:31,835
I don't want to wait for
a moment.

988
01:53:31,835 --> 01:53:34,605
I won't sleep before hurting Osman.

989
01:53:34,605 --> 01:53:37,335
Then, you won't stay sleepless
for long.

990
01:53:37,555 --> 01:53:41,805
Because, our first job will be
destroying that headquarters.

991
01:54:04,785 --> 01:54:06,385
You summoned me, master.

992
01:54:19,785 --> 01:54:22,005
What did Osman Bey do?

993
01:54:22,005 --> 01:54:24,155
He made Bilecik home for the Turks!

994
01:54:24,155 --> 01:54:28,275
-What did Osman Bey do?
-Killed the tyrant!

995
01:54:28,435 --> 01:54:30,135
What did Osman Bey do?

996
01:54:30,135 --> 01:54:32,705
He saved the oppressed!

997
01:54:32,705 --> 01:54:34,455
What did Osman Bey do?

998
01:54:34,455 --> 01:54:37,455
He opened the door for many
conquests!

999
01:54:37,505 --> 01:55:01,505
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

1000
01:55:03,305 --> 01:55:12,805
On this sacred Ramadan night, we are
grateful to Allah for this destiny!

1001
01:55:18,755 --> 01:55:20,205
Bilecik Castle...

1002
01:55:21,535 --> 01:55:22,955
belongs to the Turks now!

1003
01:55:23,035 --> 01:55:34,555
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

1004
01:55:36,835 --> 01:55:39,085
We'll have our sahur meal
here, right?

1005
01:55:39,685 --> 01:55:41,055
We will.

1006
01:55:44,705 --> 01:55:51,755
We'll eat our sahur and iftar meals in
many places together.

1007
01:55:51,755 --> 01:55:53,755
Inshallah.

1008
01:56:03,385 --> 01:56:05,105
Bilecik Castle...

1009
01:56:07,235 --> 01:56:13,235
will belong to the Turks and Islam
forever!

1010
01:56:43,785 --> 01:56:46,285
The flag of the Turks will wave!

1011
01:56:47,285 --> 01:56:50,785
The sounds of our azans will
not be silenced!

1012
01:56:52,235 --> 01:56:57,305
Our iftars and sahurs will be done
in these lands.

1013
01:56:58,305 --> 01:56:59,805
Brothers!

1014
01:57:01,505 --> 01:57:03,085
Valiants!

1015
01:57:04,435 --> 01:57:06,185
This is a difficult road.

1016
01:57:07,785 --> 01:57:09,785
But you weren't afraid.

1017
01:57:10,605 --> 01:57:12,105
Thank you.

1018
01:57:12,955 --> 01:57:15,205
You always stood with us.

1019
01:57:16,405 --> 01:57:18,535
And you made the conquest
easier.

1020
01:57:26,755 --> 01:57:28,305
Hatuns.

1021
01:57:29,585 --> 01:57:32,125
You always stood behind me.

1022
01:57:33,665 --> 01:57:35,215
Thank you.

1023
01:57:35,315 --> 01:57:36,885
We did.

1024
01:57:39,005 --> 01:57:41,025
We don't want to anymore.

1025
01:57:41,205 --> 01:57:43,775
We want to run after conquests now.

1026
01:57:46,785 --> 01:57:48,325
We won't stand.

1027
01:57:48,915 --> 01:57:53,705
We'll dream for more, as long
as we breath.

1028
01:57:53,895 --> 01:57:55,595
Inshallah, my bey.

1029
01:57:55,675 --> 01:57:58,465
We'll raise our children
with that dream.

1030
01:57:58,705 --> 01:58:00,275
Inshallah.

1031
01:58:04,945 --> 01:58:07,465
Our target is İnegöl.

1032
01:58:07,745 --> 01:58:13,775
This Friday, we'll be together
next to İnegöl walls.

1033
01:58:14,475 --> 01:58:18,755
And inshallah, we'll do our iftar
in İnegöl.

1034
01:58:19,455 --> 01:58:21,985
It's time for conquest now!

1035
01:58:22,765 --> 01:58:26,845
Bilecik Castle belongs to the Turks!

1036
01:58:28,405 --> 01:58:33,475
But never forget!

1037
01:58:35,415 --> 01:58:37,505
We are only holding them for now.

1038
01:58:38,885 --> 01:58:41,675
Everything belongs to Allah only.

1039
01:58:42,705 --> 01:58:47,785
We fight and conquest for Allah.

1040
01:58:52,115 --> 01:58:57,195
Until there is no place without
Allah's name...

1041
01:59:01,335 --> 01:59:02,915
Allahu Akbar!

1042
01:59:03,175 --> 01:59:26,435
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

1043
01:59:26,525 --> 01:59:28,075
Allahu Akbar!

1044
01:59:28,275 --> 01:59:42,865
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

1045
02:00:14,585 --> 02:00:16,295
Sheik Edebalı...

1046
02:00:16,845 --> 02:00:19,055
while you are fasting...

1047
02:00:20,695 --> 02:00:24,305
I won't feel good about having this soup.

1048
02:00:26,105 --> 02:00:29,755
You'll drink, Kosses.
It's to heal you.

1049
02:00:32,795 --> 02:00:38,105
Know that, Islam cares about human life
more than anything else.

1050
02:00:39,285 --> 02:00:43,375
You need to have this soup for
your health.

1051
02:00:44,275 --> 02:00:49,545
Once you have it, we'll acquire merit.

1052
02:00:50,125 --> 02:00:52,975
You'll be helping us.

1053
02:01:00,425 --> 02:01:02,965
If you say so...

1054
02:01:14,215 --> 02:01:16,765
Thank you, Selcan Hatun.

1055
02:01:17,865 --> 02:01:19,675
May it heal you.

1056
02:01:21,675 --> 02:01:24,875
Osman loves that soup.

1057
02:01:26,825 --> 02:01:31,035
Now I know the secret behind
Osman's victories.

1058
02:01:31,965 --> 02:01:34,105
Not at all.

1059
02:01:36,685 --> 02:01:39,205
I wanted to see them...

1060
02:01:40,785 --> 02:01:43,065
return safe and sound.

1061
02:01:48,175 --> 02:01:51,095
My Allah who made the
conquest of Bilecik easy...

1062
02:01:51,475 --> 02:01:55,855
will make their return to
the tribe easy too.

1063
02:01:56,745 --> 02:01:58,635
With Allah's approval,
you'll see them.

1064
02:01:58,755 --> 02:02:00,775
Be at ease.

1065
02:02:00,975 --> 02:02:03,855
Inshallah.
Inshallah, my sheik.

1066
02:02:16,845 --> 02:02:18,775
Osman Bey is coming.

1067
02:02:22,625 --> 02:02:24,935
Thank Allah, he is here.

1068
02:02:26,005 --> 02:02:27,805
My valiants are here.

1069
02:02:28,055 --> 02:02:29,915
With the name of Allah.

1070
02:02:40,375 --> 02:02:42,125
My valiants are here.

1071
02:02:51,285 --> 02:02:53,175
Osman Bey is coming!

1072
02:02:58,845 --> 02:03:02,735
My Allah destined him with conquest.

1073
02:03:03,045 --> 02:03:05,755
We are grateful forever...

1074
02:03:05,865 --> 02:03:09,415
for protecting our children.

1075
02:03:17,065 --> 02:03:19,385
Thank you!

1076
02:03:19,385 --> 02:03:21,845
Welcome, my bey!

1077
02:03:22,235 --> 02:03:25,495
Thank you!
Thank you!

1078
02:03:25,915 --> 02:03:29,585
Thank you!

1079
02:03:41,225 --> 02:03:43,445
Welcome, my bey!

1080
02:03:48,635 --> 02:03:50,635
O' people!

1081
02:03:52,325 --> 02:03:57,315
Bilecik Castle now belongs to the Kayı!

1082
02:03:57,665 --> 02:04:22,675
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

1083
02:04:23,105 --> 02:04:28,095
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

1084
02:04:28,095 --> 02:04:30,175
Osman...

1085
02:04:30,385 --> 02:04:31,905
Osman...

1086
02:04:32,115 --> 02:04:33,635
Mother?

1087
02:04:33,835 --> 02:04:35,895
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

1088
02:04:40,315 --> 02:04:41,645
Mother!

1089
02:04:41,775 --> 02:04:43,515
Mother Selcan!

1090
02:04:43,865 --> 02:04:46,425
Mother! Mother!

1091
02:04:46,425 --> 02:04:48,455
Mother Selcan!

1092
02:04:49,115 --> 02:04:52,655
Mother! Mother!

1093
02:04:53,005 --> 02:04:54,815
Mother!

1094
02:04:56,135 --> 02:04:58,955
Mother, are you alright?
Bring some water!

1095
02:05:00,315 --> 02:05:01,625
Mother!

1096
02:05:10,235 --> 02:05:12,535
Drink it.

1097
02:05:14,585 --> 02:05:16,625
Drink it. Drink it.

1098
02:05:21,565 --> 02:05:26,075
It's time to hand over the trust, son.

1099
02:05:27,805 --> 02:05:29,265
Mother...

1100
02:05:30,515 --> 02:05:32,015
Orhan...

1101
02:05:33,765 --> 02:05:36,275
Alahaddin...
Where are they?

1102
02:05:39,625 --> 02:05:43,475
My children...

1103
02:05:53,345 --> 02:05:57,175
Always protect each other.

1104
02:05:59,035 --> 02:06:02,195
Follow the path of your
ancestors.

1105
02:06:02,985 --> 02:06:07,855
Watch out for each other.

1106
02:06:08,205 --> 02:06:09,755
I promise, grandmother.

1107
02:06:23,785 --> 02:06:26,355
Kayı's brave women.

1108
02:06:31,745 --> 02:06:34,295
I'm leaving you behind...

1109
02:06:35,595 --> 02:06:38,105
so, I'm not concerned.

1110
02:06:41,685 --> 02:06:45,215
You'll expand the state...

1111
02:06:46,155 --> 02:06:50,655
as you raise your children.

1112
02:06:56,075 --> 02:07:03,635
You'll always make things easier
for Osman.

1113
02:07:09,365 --> 02:07:11,895
Give me your blessing, mother.

1114
02:07:12,555 --> 02:07:14,955
It's yours, my pretty girl.

1115
02:07:17,945 --> 02:07:20,135
Give me your blessing, mother.

1116
02:07:20,635 --> 02:07:22,635
It's yours, my pretty girl.

1117
02:07:34,625 --> 02:07:35,995
Mother.

1118
02:07:36,735 --> 02:07:38,125
Yes.

1119
02:07:38,155 --> 02:07:40,175
I made many mistakes.

1120
02:07:40,845 --> 02:07:42,935
I broke your heart.

1121
02:07:43,755 --> 02:07:45,765
Did you forgive me?

1122
02:07:45,995 --> 02:07:47,815
Gündüz.

1123
02:07:48,525 --> 02:07:50,895
I know your heart.

1124
02:07:51,415 --> 02:07:54,275
You never break any heart
knowingly.

1125
02:07:56,695 --> 02:07:59,815
You have my blessing.

1126
02:08:01,815 --> 02:08:06,475
Always watch your brother's back.

1127
02:08:19,725 --> 02:08:21,115
Osman.

1128
02:08:21,115 --> 02:08:22,235
Mother.

1129
02:08:22,235 --> 02:08:23,505
Son.

1130
02:08:23,505 --> 02:08:24,655
Mother.

1131
02:08:24,825 --> 02:08:27,385
Be at ease.

1132
02:08:28,075 --> 02:08:30,585
My time is over.

1133
02:08:37,465 --> 02:08:39,225
Gündoğdu.

1134
02:08:39,865 --> 02:08:42,665
Gündoğdu is waiting for me.

1135
02:08:44,845 --> 02:08:52,625
And a great state awaits you
with many victories.

1136
02:08:58,465 --> 02:09:05,055
May Allah keep you on the right
way.

1137
02:09:07,705 --> 02:09:09,745
Don't be sad.

1138
02:09:13,755 --> 02:09:17,465
Don't be sad, son.
Don't be sad.

1139
02:09:19,095 --> 02:09:30,065
On the eternal path, we'll
meet again, inshallah.

1140
02:09:30,825 --> 02:09:35,405
I bear witness that there is no god
but Allah...

1141
02:09:35,885 --> 02:09:43,455
and I bear witness that Muhammad is
the servant and Messenger of Allah.

1142
02:10:15,585 --> 02:10:16,945
Mother.

1143
02:10:35,065 --> 02:10:36,595
Mother.

1144
02:10:37,405 --> 02:10:39,595
You were like this as a boy too.

1145
02:10:40,295 --> 02:10:43,875
You would go, be alone when
you have trouble.

1146
02:10:44,915 --> 02:10:47,735
You would understand it and
come to me.

1147
02:10:49,595 --> 02:10:52,175
You would cure my pain
as a motherless child.

1148
02:10:52,925 --> 02:10:54,945
How can I repay you, mother.

1149
02:10:55,375 --> 02:10:57,735
What payment between a mother
and a child, son?

1150
02:10:57,855 --> 02:11:00,145
I cured your longing
for a mother...

1151
02:11:00,285 --> 02:11:03,385
and you cured my longing
for a child.

1152
02:11:04,605 --> 02:11:06,125
Mother.

1153
02:11:35,115 --> 02:11:37,385
Now, it'll be more difficult for you.

1154
02:11:38,135 --> 02:11:41,355
It's time to repair what you've
broken.

1155
02:11:47,015 --> 02:11:49,395
I separated you from
your child.

1156
02:11:50,455 --> 02:11:52,465
Give me your blessing, my girl.

1157
02:11:53,285 --> 02:11:55,015
It's yours, mother.

1158
02:12:23,605 --> 02:12:29,605
Thank Allah! Thank Allah!

1159
02:12:49,185 --> 02:12:51,775
Will you take good care
of my daughter?

1160
02:12:52,265 --> 02:12:54,085
I will, mother.

1161
02:12:55,435 --> 02:12:57,295
I give my permission!

1162
02:13:03,355 --> 02:13:07,025
-My pretty girl.
-So glad I have you, mother.

1163
02:13:07,835 --> 02:13:09,945
So glad we have you.

1164
02:13:10,185 --> 02:13:11,925
Always, my girl.

1165
02:13:12,165 --> 02:13:14,245
Go to your mother.

1166
02:13:14,655 --> 02:13:16,395
My son!

1167
02:13:19,785 --> 02:13:21,545
Mother.

1168
02:13:26,565 --> 02:13:30,855
''Verily we belong to Allah and verily to
Him do we return.''

1169
02:13:53,745 --> 02:13:56,245
End of the episode 91

